# Sway — default session ("Sway", "Sway 1.11", "Sway (Nvidia)")
#
# This is the config every login-screen entry loads except Sway(fonn), and
# "Sway (Nvidia)" — /usr/local/bin/sway-nvidia, which takes no -c — is the one
# that actually gets used, so treat this as the Nvidia desk.
#
# sway-nvidia used to be the apt sway 1.9 / wlroots 0.17 stack. That is what was
# causing the flickering: wlroots 0.17 has no explicit sync
# (linux-drm-syncobj-v1), and the Dell hangs off card1-HDMI-A-1, i.e. the NVIDIA
# GPU, so the driver and the compositor disagreed about when a buffer was safe
# to scan out. It now delegates to /opt/sway-next/bin/sway-next-session — Sway
# 1.11 / wlroots 0.19, which has explicit sync and runs the Vulkan renderer.
# The plain "Sway" entry is still apt 1.9 and is the rollback.
#
# Everything shared with the other sway sessions lives in `common` — bindings,
# modes, colors, window rules, daemons. Edit that and every session picks it up.
# Edit THIS file only for what should be true here and nowhere else.
#
# For the work desk, see profiles/fonn.config and pick "Sway(fonn)" at the login
# screen.

include common

### Screens — 1 terminal · 2 zen · 3 discord+slack · 4 ticktick+spotify · 5 obsidian
#
# WHICH app goes on which screen is not written here — it lives in
#   ~/.config/sway-layouts/default.layout   (-> dot_files/layouts/default.layout)
# so the layout can change without touching sway config or reloading sway.
exec $HOME/.local/bin/sway-layout default

### VPN
# Idempotent: does nothing if the tunnel is already up in Seattle, and moves it
# if it is up somewhere else. It waits for DNS first — sway's exec fires before
# NetworkManager is necessarily usable, and a bare `nordvpn connect` loses that
# race at login and fails silently, leaving you unprotected.
#
# Not in default.layout because that file is about which app owns which screen,
# and this opens no window.
exec $HOME/.local/bin/vpn-connect United_States Seattle

### Window rules
# Thunderbird has no screen of its own here — Mod+minus summons it. TickTick
# does have one (screen 4), which is why its scratchpad rule is not in `common`
# any more but in the one profile that wants it, fonn.config.
for_window [app_id="thunderbird"] move scratchpad

### Daemons
exec kanshi
